WEBVTT

NOTE Descriptive captions for a silent screen recording. Cue times follow the on-screen section changes.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
[No sound] Every AI agent. One workspace you own.

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:09.500
Projects: give the coordinator a goal.

3
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:15.000
It starts a worker for each part and lists them in the Threads rail.

4
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Each job gets the model that fits.

5
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:25.000
Here Codex writes tip.py while Claude writes the README.

6
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:31.000
Results come back to one conversation. The coordinator checks each worker's output against the goal.

7
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:38.000
Hit a limit? The usage view shows every account's limits.

8
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:48.000
When Claude runs out, Continue with Codex carries the conversation over, so Codex knows the code word only Claude was told. The limit in this clip is simulated.

9
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:56.000
One record in git. The open-source specweave CLI hands off at 90% of a usage window, and any agent continues with specweave pickup.

10
00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:01.000
Bring your agents. Keep your machines. spec-weave.com/studio
